        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "EO 10397 (17 FR 8605; signed September 25, 1952; F.R. Doc. 52-10565) continues in effect, under section 1(c) of the Emergency Powers Continuation Act (66 Stat. 333), until and including April 1, 1953 all appointments as officers and warrant officers of the Army and Air Force that would terminate after April 27, 1952 and before April 1, 1953 under three listed provisions of law. The first end is the own-terms date April 1, 1953. The order's own words run the continuation until and including that date, so the date is inclusive and no exclusive reading is needed. The end source is the held Federal Register text of the order itself (the order's registered original); the packet's wording leads for this order come from a text without a graded fragment record and are not used.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"The packet's number-citation lookup lists no held order citing EO 10397 other than its own Federal Register page, and the later-events catalog search has no hit for it, so no held instrument revokes, supersedes, extends or amends it. The statute it relies on is cited only as the authority; the packet holds no text that ends the statutory authority before April 1, 1953.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"The order appoints no one and delegates nothing; it only extends the duration of existing appointments, so no independent command survives April 1, 1953.\",\"savings_check\":\"Appointments continued through April 1, 1953 were in effect during that period, and service and acts under them are accrued. The order itself continues no appointment past April 1, 1953.\",\"scope_check\":\"One operative clause. The three enumerated items identify which appointments are continued; they are not separate commands and share the single end date.\"}",
